- op: discuss  # ac4e
  at: '2026-08-11T12:38:21Z'  # ac4e
  by: agent  # ac4e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ac4e
  clock: 4  # ac4e
  nonce: ac4e  # ac4e
  message: "DONE via resolution (2), the repo_inspection zone, per the owner's ruling.\n\nWHAT LANDED. Three wrappers in safety_zones.py, each invoking the zone barrier:\n  repo_inspect_git    local read-only git   (repo_fingerprint.py, sketch_embeddings.py)\n  repo_inspect_scan   gitleaks secret scan  (gitleaks.py)\n  repo_inspect_probe  rust-analyzer --version (rust_analyzer_install.py, availability\n                                               check only; install/uninstall runners\n                                               are extras-path and out of scope)\nNew docs/hypergumbo-self-catalog/repo_inspection_sinks.yaml declares all three in\nzone repo_inspection, registered in claims.yaml extra_catalogs. The existing\nzone_barrier_sanitizers.yaml already covers _safety_zone_barrier for\nruntime_cli_entry, so no sanitizer change was needed.\n\nTHREE WRAPPERS, NOT ONE, despite near-identical bodies -- mirroring the existing\ncache_write / user_out_write / tmp_artifact_write split. The taint machinery keys\non the FUNCTION, so separate names let a future claim prohibit one activity while\npermitting another. One wrapper would collapse \"reads your git metadata\" and\n\"reads every byte of your source\" into a single indistinguishable permission, and\ngitleaks is the member a user with a private repo would actually want disclosed.\n\nCLAIM RESTATED, NOT SOFTENED. The new text enumerates exactly what is permitted,\nstates that anything else (curl, pip, rustup, an unwrapped call) is prohibited,\nand NAMES ITS OWN PREVIOUS WORDING AS FALSE with the strace evidence, rather than\nquietly deleting the sentence that was wrong.\n\nBEHAVIOUR IS BYTE-IDENTICAL, WHICH IS THE POINT. The strace canary re-run after\nthe change: git x25, gitleaks x1, rust-analyzer --version x1 -- same binaries,\nsame counts. Nothing added, removed or gated. The capability was made VISIBLE to\nthe analysis, not altered. A change to this claim that also changed behaviour\nwould have been two things at once and neither verifiable.\n\nMEASURED (hypergumbo's own tree):\n  runtime-cli-no-subprocess  violated -> inconclusive\n    1110 raw / 33 distinct unsanitized -> 0 unsanitized\n    verify-claims' own details: \"390 flow(s) reach that zone but pass through a\n    sanitizer on every route\"\n  Self-claim tally across this whole work: {violated 2, inconclusive 16} at the\n  start -> {inconclusive 18} now.\n\nZERO VIOLATED IS NOT \"PROVEN SAFE\", and confirmed is still 0. Every verdict is\ninconclusive because this repo contains bash/csharp/solidity with no taint\ncatalogue, so a negative cannot be confirmed. SECURITY.md regenerates to say\nexactly that and now publishes the enumerated repo-inspection surface.\n\nTHE ITEM'S FILED \"NOT DETERMINED\" IS ANSWERED, and answered WIDER than filed:\ngitleaks does reach a runtime subcommand and runs a real scan; rust-analyzer is\nalso reached (not on the item's list at all) but only for --version; curl / pip /\nrustup are not reached on this path. A third git call site exists that neither\nrecorded path named -- sketch_embeddings.py:1349, config --get remote.origin.url.\n\nBUILD.RS IS THE LOAD-BEARING DISTINCTION AND IS PINNED BY A TEST. rust-analyzer\nexecutes the analysed project's build.rs and proc macros when it INDEXES; the\nwhole difference between safe and not is --version versus an index request.\nTestTheProbeDoesNotIndex fails if analysis-stats / scip / lsif / diagnostics ever\nappear at that site, and its docstring says that a red there means SECURITY.md is\nwrong.\n\nDEFERRED WITH AN EXPLICIT RE-EVALUATION TRIGGER (a KEEP verdict needs one): the\n--version probe shares the zone with git and gitleaks, which is the weakest part\nof the grouping -- what unites the three is what they CANNOT do (no host write,\nno network action on the user's behalf, no execution of repository code), not\nwhat they read. A separate tool_probe zone was considered and deferred because no\nclaim today needs to prohibit the probe while permitting git. IF ANYTHING IS EVER\nADDED TO THIS ZONE THAT READS REPOSITORY CONTENT AND ACTS ON IT -- rather than\nreporting on it -- SPLIT THE ZONE BEFORE ADDING IT."  # ac4e
